  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to the `OrderPlaced` event, but I didn't remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` yet. Billing-service and analytics-ingest still read those fields, and the architecture rules (ARCH-4) say changes to this event must not break them: renames have to go through deprecation. Dropping the old names now would break both services.\n\n**What changed**\n- `src/core/events.ts`: `OrderPlaced` now has `createdAt` and `amountCents`. `placedAt` and `totalCents` are still sent with the same values and are marked `@deprecated`, with a note saying they stay until both consumers have switched.\n- `test/app.test.ts`: the tests now expect both the new and old fields.\n- I left `schemaVersion` at 3. The change only adds fields, and a consumer that checks for `=== 3` would break if I bumped it.\n- I didn't change the HTTP responses, which still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. Your request was about the event, and `GET /orders/{id}` has to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n\nAll 39 tests pass. The dependency checks report no violations (they ignore one known violation that was already there).\n\n**To finish the rename**\n1. Billing-service and analytics-ingest switch to reading `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n2. Once both are deployed, a follow-up change removes `totalCents` and `placedAt`. That removal is a breaking change, so it's probably the point to bump `schemaVersion` to 4.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Do you want me to commit this, or draft a deprecation notice for the billing and analytics teams?",
